  "deviations": [
    "Map points are sampled real detections; the sample count is shown and no synthetic points are used.",
    "Briefing rail shows the design RUN-0412 sample; the live stream is a TODO(api) boundary.",
    "Evidence uses the five published PNGs, not native SVG builders.",
    "Globe silhouettes are merged focus-country coverage from the 110m atlas; the design merges 50m at runtime.",
    "The orbit rings are decorative and labelled \"Illustration, not a measurement\".",
    "The island reference markers (Hoàng Sa, Trường Sa) are not ported.",
    "The loader runs on the landing only; the Workbench is server-rendered.",
    "Landing entry opens the last measured epoch (2025).",
    "Landing CTAs stack full width on desktop to avoid a wrapped label.",
    "The WebGL fallback is a flat equirectangular SVG map.",
    "The calendar, epoch selector and physics filter bar are the horizontal scrollers on mobile; each scrolls inside its pane.",
    "Review is shipped with the design fixture runs; the queue, run, dialogs and audit replace the endpoints behind seven TODO(api) markers.",
    "The Workbench briefing rail shows the design RUN-0412 sample; it does not yet regenerate a run from the selected region and epoch.",
    "The H3 heatmap bins the sampled projected points in screen space at Res 4–8; the analysis grid is Res 7 or 8 as selected. The full slices supply the filter counts.",
    "Map filters hide flagged sampled points; the KPI and artifact counts remain the full measured epoch because they come from the precomputed artifact.",
    "The SAA display zone is the design ellipse; the harmonization core uses the broader NASA FIRMS envelope for rejection. Both use the same thermal false-alarm rule.",
    "Service states, connect steps and the run stream are simulated locally. The token handshake and stream are the TODO(api) boundary.",
    "The globe captures one frame on arrival and morphs it into the map pane; the return trip is still a route change.",
    "The Workbench route is /workbench/[zone]; /workbench?region=… redirects to the zone path and preserves epoch/tour.",
    "The map uses a pre-projected 1000×730 SVG with client-side pan/zoom and client-side H3 bins. The design rebuilds a d3 projection per resize.",
    "The lens is a true-scale SVG built from the published physics values; the map footprints are ellipses from FIRMS scan/track, clamped at low zoom."
  ]
}
